# Got It All's reply kinds against rival containers (task 8 review lesson: the Whitegate NPCs have no script, so a lone
# reply shows no kind; the trace shows that a Progress beats an Event and that equal kinds rotate by the last event
# played, even across a finish and a state reset, so each pair or triple of triggers has a rival and the state its
# finish moves is reset between them). One char per scenario.
# Tehf Kimasnahya against Three Men and a Closet 843 (Progress, Prog 3) and 844 (Event, Prog 4 or completed): Got It
# All 520 (Progress, available) with 843, 527 (Progress, Prog 6) and 539 (Event, Prog 7 with the zoning flag) with 844,
# 528 (Progress, Prog 7) with 843, 525 (Progress, Prog 4) with the completed 844.
# Ekhu Pesshyadha against The Die Is Cast 592 (Progress, step 0): 522 (Progress), 537 (Event), 531 (Event).
# Zabahf against Arts and Crafts 512 (Progress, its bit 3 clear): 533 (Event, available and Prog 1 / 4), 523
# (Progress), 538 / 540 / 535 (Events).
lists AhtUrhganWhitegate/Tehf_Kimasnahya/onTrigger AhtUrhganWhitegate/Ekhu_Pesshyadha/onTrigger AhtUrhganWhitegate/Zabahf/onTrigger
